1	#!/usr/bin/env node
2	// The capture step (grow_with_claudinite pack): push this session's conversation
3	// onto the repo's orphan `conversation-logs` branch as one JSONL file named
4	// `<stamp>--issue-<n>--<session>.jsonl` (README.md owns the standard). Two events
5	// invoke it — merge-to-main, with the issue the merge closed, and the SessionEnd
6	// hook (session-end.mjs), with `--issue 0`.
7	//
8	// Delta-aware, keyed on the SESSION ID: every capture refetches the branch tip,
9	// finds all prior files for this session (whatever event or issue produced them),
10	// takes the max entry timestamp across them, and pushes only the entries strictly
11	// after it. Zero delta ⇒ no file, no commit, no push. Double-writing is therefore
12	// safe BY CONSTRUCTION — any two capture events for one session chain into
13	// disjoint files — which is the property the SessionEnd hook relies on, so
14	// pack.test.mjs pins it directly. One file maps 1:1 to a CAPTURE EVENT, not to a
15	// merge, and the nightly extract never re-reads a turn.
16	//
17	// All branch writes go through git plumbing (hash-object/mktree/commit-tree/push)
18	// against the fetched remote tip — the user's checkout and index are never
19	// touched, and there is no worktree to clean up.
20	//
21	// Usage (from the repo root, right after the merge lands):
22	//   node capture-log.mjs --issue <n> [--transcript <path>] [--branch <name>] [--session <id>]
23	//
24	// The session id (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, or --session) names the transcript file
25	// exactly, so discovery searches every project directory for it — a remote/web
26	// session's transcript can land under a slug the git-root path never reproduces.
27	
28	import { readFileSync, readdirSync, existsSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';
